{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"shell-snippets","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.1.0","displayName":"Shell Script Snippets","description":"Safe Bash scripts: strict mode, argument parsing, loops, traps and checks.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Snippets"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","contributes":{"snippets":[{"language":"Shell","path":"snippets/shell.json"}]}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"snippets/shell.json":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"{\n  \"Bash header\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"bash\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"#!/usr/bin/env bash\",\n      \"set -euo pipefail\",\n      \"\",\n      \"$0\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A strict Bash script\"\n  },\n  \"If\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"if\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"if [[ ${1:condition} ]]; then\",\n      \"\\t$0\",\n      \"fi\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"if\"\n  },\n  \"If else\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"ife\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"if [[ ${1:condition} ]]; then\",\n      \"\\t$2\",\n      \"else\",\n      \"\\t$0\",\n      \"fi\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"if else\"\n  },\n  \"For loop\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"for\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"for ${1:item} in ${2:items}; do\",\n      \"\\t$0\",\n      \"done\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"for in\"\n  },\n  \"While read\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"wr\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"while IFS= read -r ${1:line}; do\",\n      \"\\t$0\",\n      \"done < \\\"${2:file}\\\"\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Read lines\"\n  },\n  \"Function\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"fn\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"${1:name}() {\",\n      \"\\tlocal ${2:arg}=\\\"\\\\${1:-}\\\"\",\n      \"\\t$0\",\n      \"}\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A function\"\n  },\n  \"Case\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"case\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"case \\\"\\\\$${1:var}\\\" in\",\n      \"\\t${2:pattern}) $0 ;;\",\n      \"\\t*) ;;\",\n      \"esac\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"case\"\n  },\n  \"Usage check\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"usage\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"if [[ \\\\$# -lt ${1:1} ]]; then\",\n      \"\\techo \\\"usage: \\\\$0 ${2:<arg>}\\\" >&2\",\n      \"\\texit 1\",\n      \"fi\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Check arguments\"\n  },\n  \"Trap cleanup\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"trap\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"cleanup() {\",\n      \"\\t$0\",\n      \"}\",\n      \"trap cleanup EXIT\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Clean up on exit\"\n  },\n  \"Command exists\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"cmd\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"command -v ${1:git} >/dev/null 2>&1 || { echo \\\"${1:git} is required\\\" >&2; exit 1; }\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"Check a command\"\n  },\n  \"Script directory\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"dir\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"SCRIPT_DIR=\\\"$(cd \\\"$(dirname \\\"\\\\${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\\\")\\\" && pwd)\\\"\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"The directory of the script\"\n  },\n  \"Default value\": {\n    \"prefix\": \"def\",\n    \"body\": [\n      \"${1:NAME}=\\\"\\\\${${1:NAME}:-${2:default}}\\\"\"\n    ],\n    \"description\": \"A default value\"\n  }\n}\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Shell Script Snippets\n\nSafe Bash scripts: strict mode, argument parsing, loops, traps and checks.\n\nType a prefix and press Tab. 12 snippets.\n\n| Language | Prefix | What it inserts |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Shell | `bash` | A strict Bash script |\n| Shell | `if` | if |\n| Shell | `ife` | if else |\n| Shell | `for` | for in |\n| Shell | `wr` | Read lines |\n| Shell | `fn` | A function |\n| Shell | `case` | case |\n| Shell | `usage` | Check arguments |\n| Shell | `trap` | Clean up on exit |\n| Shell | `cmd` | Check a command |\n| Shell | `dir` | The directory of the script |\n| Shell | `def` | A default value |\n\nThis extension runs no code and asks for no permissions.\n"}}}